From: Josip Seketa <josip.seketa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:10:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 24/43] gdbserver: wait for the attached thread's SIGSTOP in
 all-stop attach

Waiting for any thread left the leader's SIGSTOP pending (attach-into-signal.exp).

diff --git a/gdbserver/server.cc b/gdbserver/server.cc
index 90307c38b50..99127d0e010 100644
--- a/gdbserver/server.cc
+++ b/gdbserver/server.cc
@@ -318,7 +318,14 @@ attach_inferior (int pid)
 
   if (!non_stop)
     {
-      cs.last_ptid = mywait (ptid_t (pid), &cs.last_status, 0, 0);
+      /* Wait for the SIGSTOP of the thread we attached to first; see
+	 linux_process_target::attach.  Another thread may have a
+	 signal to report too, and taking that one instead would leave
+	 the SIGSTOP pending as if the program had got it: it would be
+	 reported later, and delivered to the program on detach.  The
+	 other thread's event stays pending and is reported on the next
+	 resume.  */
+      cs.last_ptid = mywait (ptid_t (pid, pid), &cs.last_status, 0, 0);
 
       /* GDB knows to ignore the first SIGSTOP after attaching to a running
 	 process using the "attach" command, but this is different; it's
